# What this file does: excludes paths from the Docker build context sent to the daemon
# when any image in this repo is built (`docker compose build`, CI's `docker build`).
# Used here and why: the repo root is the build context for every service's Dockerfile
# (apps/api, apps/web); without this file, VCS metadata, secrets, caches, and dev-only
# tooling would all be uploaded to the daemon and could leak into image layers or just
# slow builds down. Kept as one root-level file since there's a single build context.
# How it fits the project: docs/03-architecture.md §9 (repo layout) — apps/api and
# apps/web each have a Dockerfile but no per-app .dockerignore, so this file is what
# keeps their build contexts lean.
# Depends on: nothing. Used by: `docker build`/`docker compose build` for every service.

# VCS metadata — never needed inside an image
.git

# Secrets — must never be baked into an image layer
.env
.env.*

# Installed/build artifacts — regenerated inside the image, not copied in
**/node_modules
**/.svelte-kit
**/build
**/.venv

# Python bytecode and tool caches — machine-specific, safe to regenerate
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.pyc

# Test suite and package-manager store — not needed at runtime
apps/api/tests
.pnpm-store

# Repo tooling/docs not needed inside any image
.superpowers
.agentmaster
docs
